<!-- A fountain-pen nib whose ink channel is a circuit: two shoulder nodes feed
     the breather hole, and the slit runs from it clean through the tip.

     The slit reaching the tip is the whole identity — stopped short, the same
     silhouette reads as a shield. Everything else is kept thin on purpose: the
     traces are 2.8 wide against a 35-wide body, because thicker ones hollow the
     nib out and it stops looking like metal at launcher size.

     Drawn as ink first, then the channel painted back over it in the background
     colour. The alternative (evenOdd holes) fills black again wherever a node
     overlaps a trace, which is everywhere. Both layers of the adaptive icon are
     always composited together, so the two colours cannot drift apart.

     Furthest point from centre is the shoulder at (36.5, 27.5): radius 31.75,
     inside the 33 safe circle a launcher mask is allowed to cut to. -->
